    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 321\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7912-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the New York state urban development corporation\n      act, in relation to extending the amount of time between notice of\n      a project and a public hearing\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would increase the notice period for  all  capital  projects\npursued by the Urban Development Corporation (\"UDC\") from 10 to 20 days,\ndelaying  the  timeframe under which UDC may sell or lease certain land.\nIt would also extend the required notice period for  mandatory  hearings\nheld by municipalities when UDC needs to acquire property from a munici-\npality in order to pursue a project.\n\n  This  bill  would  result in inefficient delay that is contrary to the\npurpose of the existing UDC Act. Indeed, the Legislature amended the UDC\nAct twenty-five years ago specifically to reduce  and  streamline  these\nvery  same  hearing  requirements.  L. 1990, c.732. Extending the notice\nperiod would undo much of that work.\n \n  Moreover, lengthening the notice period for all capital projects would\nlimit UDC's ability to respond quickly to projects and communities  most\nin need of assistance, many of which are part of important gubernatorial\ninitiatives.\n \n  This  bill would make a sweeping change that would materially increase\nthe timeframe for required regulatory approvals, thereby hampering UDC's\nability to expeditiously  provide  economic  development  assistance  to\ncommunities  in need, with no evidence whatsoever that adding 10 days to\nthe notice period would increase public participation in public hearings\nor serve any other useful purpose.\n\n  I previously vetoed identical bills, as they would have served only to\ndelay the provision of economic development assistance  to  hundreds  of\nfuture  projects  throughout  the  State,  many  of them in economically\ndistressed Upstate communities (Veto Message No. 214 of 2015, No. 507 of\n2014). For the same reasons, I am compelled to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
